{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00258",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 5.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Well, you know, hello, doctor. Where would you like me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.02,
      "end_seconds": 10.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "So, that's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.08,
      "end_seconds": 16.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Uh, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.11,
      "end_seconds": 26.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.29,
      "text": "Mainly I've been getting breathless walking short distances. That's why I came. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.37,
      "end_seconds": 29.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.15,
      "end_seconds": 34.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Okay, um, so I've had it for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.98,
      "end_seconds": 45.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.34,
      "end_seconds": 60.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.84,
      "text": "It happens all the time. Mild, I'd say. I notice it more with walking uphill. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.0,
      "end_seconds": 63.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.66,
      "end_seconds": 87.96,
      "duration_seconds": 23.3,
      "text": "Um, when it starts I tend to get occasional wheeze as well. The occasional wheeze? That's been for nearly five years. With occasional wheeze, maybe a three out of ten on a bad day. Tiredness was there, um, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.42,
      "end_seconds": 93.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any night sweats, fever or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.06,
      "end_seconds": 96.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.83,
      "end_seconds": 101.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Alright, any chest pain or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.67,
      "end_seconds": 103.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.8,
      "end_seconds": 106.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.11,
      "end_seconds": 108.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.89,
      "end_seconds": 113.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.86,
      "end_seconds": 116.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Right, no, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.62,
      "end_seconds": 118.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.11,
      "end_seconds": 123.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.64,
      "end_seconds": 125.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.97,
      "end_seconds": 129.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.59,
      "end_seconds": 136.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.45,
      "end_seconds": 140.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Asthma, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.98,
      "end_seconds": 144.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Okay. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.92,
      "end_seconds": 149.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Right, I had my tonsils out when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.08,
      "end_seconds": 156.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.98,
      "end_seconds": 160.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Asthalin inhaler, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.06,
      "end_seconds": 165.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.8,
      "end_seconds": 170.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Right, um, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.46,
      "end_seconds": 177.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.53,
      "end_seconds": 179.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Yes, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.45,
      "end_seconds": 182.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.96,
      "end_seconds": 197.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "There are fine crackles at the bases of both lungs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.45,
      "end_seconds": 200.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.35,
      "end_seconds": 215.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "No clubbing in the fingers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.64,
      "end_seconds": 217.34,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.33,
      "end_seconds": 243.74,
      "duration_seconds": 20.41,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Putting it all together, it fits best with chronic breathlessness that needs a proper work-up. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.32,
      "end_seconds": 249.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.36,
      "end_seconds": 268.65,
      "duration_seconds": 17.29,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's chronic breathlessness that needs a proper work-up, and we'll know more once the a chest X-ray is back. Let's get a chest X-ray, for chronic breathlessness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.5,
      "end_seconds": 271.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Okay, uh, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.31,
      "end_seconds": 280.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.61,
      "text": "Let's get a CT scan of the chest, for chronic breathlessness. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.49,
      "end_seconds": 283.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.82,
      "end_seconds": 289.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Try a daily walk and note how far you get before you need to stop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.21,
      "end_seconds": 301.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.02,
      "text": "Alright. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.87,
      "end_seconds": 303.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.8,
      "end_seconds": 309.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Let's review you after the results are back. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.77,
      "end_seconds": 314.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Well, that's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.21,
      "end_seconds": 317.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}